  "caveats": [
    "a >= 4 only. a = 3 has no loop pass (m would be -1) and needs its own treatment; a = 2 is excluded throughout this arc.",
    "The forced schedule follows each lineage by taking the deg-lex-greatest image word as the successor. That is a heuristic for 'which word did this term become', and it is only sound while the lineage has not split -- which is exactly what the term-count column records.",
    "Confirming a proved reduction numerically adds no logical strength. It is recorded because it checks the Lean's WORDS against the engine's: a lemma can be sorry-free and still be about the wrong monomial."
